---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site.config';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | SM Global Accounting Services"
  description="How SM Global Accounting Services collects, uses and protects personal data."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy Policy</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="lead">Last updated: [date]</p>

      <p class="placeholder-note" style="margin: var(--space-3) 0; max-width: none;">
        This page is a drafted starting template, not final legal text. It has not been reviewed by
        a solicitor and should not be published as-is. Every bracketed item needs a confirmed answer,
        and the whole document needs sign-off before it governs a live site handling real UK client
        data — see <code>LAUNCH_CHECKLIST.md</code>.
      </p>

      <div class="grid" style="max-width: 760px; margin-top: var(--space-3);">
        <div>
          <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
          <p>
            This website is operated by {SITE.name} (&ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo;), [legal entity
            name and registration details], [registered address]. We provide outsourced bookkeeping,
            statutory accounts, tax and related accounting support to UK accountancy practices. You
            can contact us at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>2. What this policy covers</h2>
          <p>
            This policy explains how we handle personal data collected through this website — for
            example, when you fill in a contact form or book a consultation. It does not cover how we
            handle client data while carrying out accounting work for a practice we're engaged by;
            that is governed separately by our engagement letter and data processing agreement with
            that practice.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>3. What we collect</h2>
          <p>Through this website, we may collect:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Contact details you give us directly — name, practice name, email address, phone number, and the content of any message you send.</li>
            <li>Basic technical data generated by visiting the site (e.g. pages viewed), [if and once analytics is added — see LAUNCH_CHECKLIST.md; none is currently in use].</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>4. How we use it</h2>
          <p>We use the information above to:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Respond to enquiries and arrange consultations.</li>
            <li>Correspond with you about a potential or existing engagement.</li>
            <li>Meet our own legal and accounting obligations.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Our legal basis for this is our legitimate interest in responding to enquiries from prospective clients, and, where an engagement follows, performance of that contract.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>5. International transfers</h2>
          <p>
            We are based in India. If you are contacting us from the UK or EU, your enquiry details
            will be transferred to and processed in India. [Confirm and state the specific safeguard
            relied on for this transfer — e.g. UK International Data Transfer Agreement / EU Standard
            Contractual Clauses — before publishing; do not leave this section vague in the final
            version.]
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>6. How long we keep it</h2>
          <p>
            We keep enquiry details for as long as needed to respond to you and, if an engagement
            follows, for the duration of that engagement plus [retention period to be confirmed] to
            meet our legal and accounting obligations.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>7. Sharing your data</h2>
          <p>
            We do not sell personal data. The contact form on this site is processed by FormSubmit
            (formsubmit.co), a third-party form-delivery service: it receives what you submit and
            forwards it straight to our inbox, without needing an account of our own with them. [Confirm
            FormSubmit's data-processing location and retention practices against their own privacy
            policy before publishing, and add a booking-tool processor here too once one is wired up —
            see <code>LAUNCH_CHECKLIST.md</code>.] Beyond that, we may share data with other service
            providers who help us run this website or our business (for example, email hosting), under
            contractual confidentiality obligations.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>8. Cookies</h2>
          <p>
            This site currently sets no analytics or marketing cookies. If that changes (for example,
            if privacy-respecting analytics is added), this section will be updated and a cookie
            consent mechanism will be added first, in line with UK PECR requirements — see
            <code>LAUNCH_CHECKLIST.md</code>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>9. Your rights</h2>
          <p>
            Depending on where you're located, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, or
            restrict our use of your personal data, and to object to or withdraw consent for
            processing. To exercise any of these, contact us at
            <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. UK-based individuals also have the
            right to complain to the Information Commissioner's Office (ICO) at ico.org.uk.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
          <p>We may update this policy from time to time. The &ldquo;last updated&rdquo; date at the top will always reflect the current version.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>11. Contact</h2>
          <p>
            Questions about this policy can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
